\pard\b\fs20 Ruf der Wipfe\b0\par
\fs16\par
Ruf der Wipfe is a large-scale settlement game. At first the Clonks have nothing but a banner and a little building know-how. But with research and industry their tribe grows into a splendid civilization with power plants, magic and government.\par
Many Clonks may well not live to see it, since ghosts, hunger and disease threaten them all along the way. A deep fall easily ends in death, too, and the environment strikes back hard at gross mistreatment.\par
The RdW universe is full of more or less visible details. Ancient ruins are discovered, and local wind currents make wind turbines take special planning.\par
\par
\b Advice for beginners:\b0\par
- A Clonk needs several things to survive. They are shown in the top left corner of the screen: the fields show the Clonk's need for food, need for sleep, health and psyche (morale). The second row shows fuel, disease and so on.\par
- Clonks can only sleep at night, and only in cabins and beds, unless they are overtired (<60%).\par
- Trading is only possible in the tavern.\par
- Pollution shows as a faint poison-green tint of the screen. Factories, waste and the like cause it, and trees and filter plants reduce it. When pollution is high, the sea level rises and the Clonks fall ill.\par
- The RdW power plants are far more effective than the power plants of the normal game.\par
